<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9900" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιδῐκ-έω</span></b> , impf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠντιδίκουν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					6.12
				</span></i>
			, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠντεδίκουν</span> (acc. to
			the best Ms.) <i><span class="en">
				D.
				39.37
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				40.18
			</span></i>: aor.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠντεδίκησα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					47.28
				</span></i>
			:—<i>to be an</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίδικος,</span>
			<i>dispute, go to law,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Mem.</u>
					4.4.8
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἀντιδικοῦντες ἑκάτεροι</span>”
				<i>the parties to a suit,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					948d
				</span></i>
			: abs., of the defendant, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντιδικῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					776
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. πρός τι</span> or 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τινα</span>”
				<i>to urge one's suit against . .,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					28.17
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				41.10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Is.
				11.9
			</span></i>; <i>join issue,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠντιδίκει ἦ μήν . .,</span> c. acc. et
				inf., Lys.l.c.; <i>oppose, rebut,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαβολαῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					41.13
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλήλοις</span> prob. in Thugen.I<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be an object of dispute,</i> Phot.<i><span class="en">
				p.147R.
			</span></i></div>
